1. Ownership
The Barbearia software, including its source code, design, documentation and
all related materials (the "Software"), is owned by Alexandro Cunha (the
"Licensor"). The Software is protected by copyright and other laws. No rights
are granted except those stated in this license.

2. Hosted use (the subscription)
A barbershop that subscribes to the hosted service receives a non-exclusive,
non-transferable, revocable right to use the Software through the Licensor's
service for its own business, while its subscription is active. Access is
governed by the Terms of Service and the subscription plan the barbershop
accepts. The barbershop does not receive a copy of the Software.

3. Self-hosting
Running the Software on infrastructure the customer controls requires a
separate written agreement with the Licensor. Without that agreement, no copy
of the Software may be installed or run outside the Licensor's service.

4. Restrictions
Unless a separate written agreement says otherwise, you may not:
a) copy, modify, translate, adapt or create derivative works of the Software;
b) sell, rent, lease, sublicense, distribute or otherwise make the Software
   available to third parties;
c) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, except where the
   law expressly allows it despite this restriction;
d) remove or alter copyright or proprietary notices;
e) use the Software to build a competing product or service;
f) use the Software for any unlawful purpose.

5. Customer content
Each barbershop keeps ownership of the data and content it enters into the
Software (its business details, photographs, services, barbers and bookings).
The Licensor processes that data only to provide the service, as described in
the Privacy Policy and the Terms of Service.

6. Open-source components
The Software uses third-party open-source components, each under its own
license. Those licenses apply to those components and are listed in the
